                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                       